WEBVTT

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.970
<i>I'll bet Akira's caught on by now.</i>

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.290
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:16.990
<b><<Trueblade>>

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.400
<i>My real ability is...</i>

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.510
<i>The ability to turn a stick into a 
sword </i>that can cut through anything<i>!</i>

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.830
<b>Episode 4   "Plagiarist"</b>

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.960
<i>If Kirisaki's sword is a sword 
that can cut through anything...</i>

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.210
<i>For someone with his kinetic 
vision and reflexes...</i>

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.920
<i>That ability's a perfect fit.</i>

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.340
Hey, girlie. You get it, don't ya?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.260
Ain't no way you can beat 
me with your ability.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.730
Why not forfeit already?

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.150
<i>If I forfeit now... there's no 
telling what Rin might do to me.</i>

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.450
I'm sorry...

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.820
But I can't afford to lose!

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.370
No forfeit, then?

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.910
Kirisaki! Finish this now!

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.630
<i>It's time to bet big...</i>

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.800
You sure you wanna go all-out like that?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.390
You gotta run out of 
those things sooner or—

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.100
<i>She cut off his escape route?</i>

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:53.230
Tryin' to hold me in one spot, huh?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.730
But you know I can just cut 
through the things, right?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.030
<i>Though... I'm not totally surrounded anyway.</i>

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.120
I'll give you my last one, too!

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.330
Told you it wouldn't work on—

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.000
Sorry... I had one more left over!

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.380
<i>I'm close enough to hit him before 
he can dodge or slice through it!</i>

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.600
He had a hidden knife?

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.980
Nothin' hidden about it.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.320
My ability lets me turn 
a stick into a sword.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.280
Stands to reason that if I got two sticks...

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.200
I can turn 'em both into swords.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.450
Two sticks?

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.160
<i>In that moment he was out of sight...</i>

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.550
I told you to forfeit already.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.680
I'm givin' you one more chance.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.550
Out with it.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.430
Thank you.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.100
The arrogance afforded you 
by your skill and confidence

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:17.900
is what's given me this opportunity.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.400
A marble? How'd it get there?

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.370
It bounced back this way!

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.730
<i>Looks like someone's unconscious!</i>

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.770
<i>Saeko Zokumyoin wins!</i>

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.190
I did it!

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.570
Hey. How'd you lose that one?

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.790
I'm starting to think 
you're kind of an idiot.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.710
<i>The ring is cleared up, so we'll resume now!</i>

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.460
<i>Akira Shiroyanagi!</i>

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.880
<i>Kouji Kitajima!</i>

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.840
<i>Please enter the ring!</i>

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.010
<i>Akira... Shiroyanagi?</i>

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.630
<i>Could he be...</i>

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.260
Hey, if you lose...

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:33.810
Yeah, they haven't told us what 
happens to the team that loses.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.770
It would be fair to assume the worst.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.770
Looks like <i>someone's</i> put me in a 
position where I can't afford to lose.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.360
Be careful.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.030
I'll do my best.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.160
<i>Just kidding.</i>

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.370
<i>There's actually no reason 
to assume the worst.</i>

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:55.200
<i>If their goal is to get 
us to kill each other,</i>

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.330
<i>it would make no sense for 
them to kill the losers.</i>

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.840
<i>They're even willing to give us medical 
treatment to make sure we can keep fighting.</i>

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.630
<i>If we do receive punishment, at least 
it won't involve killing or disabling us.</i>

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:12.220
<i>Which means my priority here isn't victory.</i>

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.020
<i>Now, please begin!</i>

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:21.770
<b><<Sophist>>

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.600
<i>What does the phrase "the 
other person" indicate?</i>

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:24.190
<b>The Other Person</b>

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.980
<i>Who of the eight people here can 
be considered "the other person"?</i>

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.030
<i>Can it apply to those on the enemy team,
other than my opponent?</i>

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.360
<i>Kirisaki, my ally?</i>

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.370
<i>Yuuri? Kumagiri?</i>

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.870
<i>If he's the only available "other person,"</i>

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.330
<i>when, precisely, is that status assigned?</i>

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.580
<i>Who, and in what exact moment, 
fulfills the condition of my ability?</i>

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.590
<i>Time to experiment.</i>

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.760
<i>First off...</i>

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.890
<i>Experiment phase one over.</i>

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.230
<i>It didn't activate, as expected.</i>

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.440
<i>I'm lucky that he didn't 
have a fast-attack ability.</i>

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.860
<i>Time to move on to phase two, then.</i>

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.360
<i>He moved!</i>

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.780
<i>But... not toward me?</i>

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.410
Kirisaki...

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.910
You still don't get it.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.120
You've almost died twice after 
underestimating your opponent.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.830
You're an incorrigible fool 
who endangered our team.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.040
At a time when I'm the only one 
capable of using an ability,

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.010
did you really think I'd let you live?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.380
<i>It activated!</i>

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.260
Wait!

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:42.900
What the...

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.820
Damn you!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.410
I wasn't serious, of course.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.660
But let that be a lesson to you.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.200
You... You actually frickin' shot at me!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.210
Please. It was a joke!

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.170
It wasn't goddamn funny!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.710
<i>He shot at his own teammate? Why?</i>

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.960
<i>Sorry, Kirisaki.</i>

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.840
<i>You've helped to clarify 
my ability's nature.</i>

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.550
<i>Good. Now it's time to 
enter the final stage.</i>

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.220
<i>This kid's a monster!</i>

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.100
<i>He's got the cannon ability?</i>

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.060
<i>I've been left behind all my life.</i>

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.980
<i>Always the sad side character.</i>

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.820
<i>Never a protagonist. 
I feared I never would be...</i>

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.150
I want to be reborn.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.080
<i>It's coming... the cannon!</i>

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.120
<i>I have to dodge it!</i>

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.290
<i>They should all think the 
cannon's my ability now.</i>

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.710
<i>I'll try them in order.</i>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.000
<i>Nothing?</i>

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.420
<i>But what about now?</i>

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.470
<i>I see.</i>

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.430
<i>So it activates under these conditions only.</i>

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.560
<i>Experiment complete.</i>

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.390
<i>Now to clip him non-lethally.</i>

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.440
<i>The blast disappeared?</i>

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.610
<i>Damn it! I showed my ability!</i>

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.540
<i>I'm dead!</i>

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:28.290
<i>It's over.</i>

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.090
<i>I'll always be a side character, 
always left behind!</i>

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.380
Keep fighting!

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.880
Keep fighting!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.180
You can still do this!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.140
<i>They're cheering... for me?</i>

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.600
<i>I've never had a girl cheer 
for me in my entire life.</i>

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.350
<i>What is this I'm feeling?</i>

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.560
Don't be silly.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.520
I'll show you how you encourage a man.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.230
Kitajima dear!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.490
If you win, these girls will do

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:55.940
<i>absolutely</i>

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.860
anything you ask!

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.570
Hey, don't tell him that!

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.130
<i>You mean it?!</i>

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.960
<i>I've been reborn!</i>

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.590
<i>I'm leaving behind my pathetic beginnings...</i>

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.340
<i>to become a protagonist!</i>

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.100
<i>A shoe?</i>

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.480
Hands up high, and hold them there.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.940
Make a move to lower them, and I shoot.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.530
At this range, I'll definitely hit first.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:41.030
When the blast disappeared, the cannon
 on my hand disappeared, too.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.080
The shoe didn't disappear, though.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.910
This proved to me that your ability...

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:49.370
It's the ability to nullify 
other abilities.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.590
But only while you have a hand 
touching the ground, right?

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.090
I... I forfeit.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:02.220
<i>The winner, Akira Shiroyanagi!</i>

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.640
<i>That was a fruitful experiment.</i>

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:15.610
<i>I started by using my ability on the people 
who thought my ability was the cannon,</i>

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.780
<i>but the cannon didn't appear.</i>

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:22.490
<i>It doesn't work if I unilaterally declare 
someone else "the other person."</i>

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.950
<i>Next, I declared I was 
going to shoot Kirisaki,</i>

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.000
<i>which established a mutual 
engagement between us.</i>

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.370
<i>The cannon activated then.</i>

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.580
<i>Once the enemy team 
had seen my ability,</i>

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.590
<i>I tried to use it, treating each of 
them as "the other person" in turn.</i>

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.510
<i>They're all my enemies,</i>

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:42.630
<i>but the cannon only activated against 
the person I was facing in the ring.</i>

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:48.020
<i>This tells me there's a condition for who my 
ability will consider "the other person."</i>

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:48.020
<b><<Sophist>>

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:52.350
<i>That it's crucial that there be an 
acknowledgment of mutual engagement</i>

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.730
<b>The other person 
about to shoot me</b>

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.730
<b>The other person 
in the ring with me</b>

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.480
<i>between myself and my target.</i>

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.280
<i>His team members outside the 
ring might see me as an enemy,</i>

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.110
<i>but they don't consider 
themselves engaged with me.</i>

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:02.320
<i>That's why it didn't activate.</i>

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:04.700
Hey! Akira!

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.330
What was all that crap about?!

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.700
<i>Oh, right. This.</i>

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.120
It was for your own good!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.250
I didn't even hit you. No big deal.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.630
It's a <i>big</i> freakin' deal!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.630
That cannon ability is pretty darn powerful.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:19.420
Yeah.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:23.260
The other man's ability seemed 
rather poor by comparison.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.220
I wouldn't say that.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:30.430
In the hands of an experienced 
fighter like you, Kumagiri,

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.930
the ability would nullify my cannon,

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.730
and I wouldn't have stood a chance.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.150
I see.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:41.110
An ability's usefulness comes 
down to who uses it, and how.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.360
<i>Match five will now begin!</i>

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.570
Guess I'm up, huh?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:50.580
Why do I seem to get stuck 
fighting all the weirdos?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.290
I've been waiting for this moment, Yuuri!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.420
<i>Yuuri Amagake!</i>

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.550
<i>Ouji Hoshino!</i>

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:01.710
<i>Please enter the ring!</i>

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:06.720
I was drowning in despair, 
thinking we'd never meet again...

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.140
But I see now that not even 
death can tear us apart!

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:22.360
That stupid piece of...

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.400
Yuuri?

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.610
You know that guy or somethin'?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.160
You freaking lived through that, too?!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.080
Calm down, Yuuri!

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.080
Get your hands off me!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.870
It's his fault I'm here!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.120
I'm gonna beat the crap out of him!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.630
Destiny has placed us together!

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.800
We'd better make it official with a wedding!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.760
Last warning, you guys...

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.300
Hands off!

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.680
Come on up.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.270
I'm gonna finish this.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.350
I'll go anywhere at all.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.520
Anywhere you ask!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.730
<i>Now, please begin!</i>

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.240
I have my doubts about this.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:09.240
Do you think Yuuri's ability 
gives her a chance?

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.660
Even if it does quintuple 
her physical abilities,

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.080
she still has the untrained 
arms of a teenage girl.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:20.040
Even quintupled, her punching power 
is unlikely to prove a threat.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.670
I don't think you have to worry.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:31.050
Stand right there, stalker asshole.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.470
Come to me, Yuuri!

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.560
Your anger, your attacks,

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:40.060
your love for me that you won't admit,
 even to yourself...

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.650
I'll absorb them all...

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.860
with my ability to make 
my body as hard as iron!

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:48.950
Oh, yeah?

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.740
Sounds a lot like my first match, then.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.990
I can beat the shit out 
of you without shame.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:56.830
She's fast!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.140
<i>The winner, Yuuri Amagake!</i>

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:19.640
If it was just her punching power quintupled, 
it might be trivial indeed.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.110
But you saw her jump in the 
waiting room, didn't you?

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.400
She has the ability to quintuple 
<i>all</i> her physical abilities.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:31.240
A punch channels all the 
muscles in the body.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:34.990
Her running speed, her muscles' extension,
 her physical strength...

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.200
If all of them are quintupled
simultaneously...

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.330
The result is amplified far 
more than five times.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.040
If that's what she can do to 
a body as hard as steel...

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:49.090
That ability of hers... 
it might be unstoppable.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.260
The end!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.680
Well done, all!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.390
The beautiful magician, Mion, returns!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.600
That's the end of the second program!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:02.600
We'll be moving on to 
the third program soon!

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.190
But first...

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.570
I have a few things to say to all of you.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.280
That's right! It's about the 
losing team's punishment!

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.740
You know you're getting penalized 
for losing this time, right?

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.620
Will we kill you all for sheer uselessness?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.950
Or did we have a clever little 
someone who's convinced himself

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:24.790
we were all paper tigers 
who'd <i>never</i> go as far

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.590
as killing anyone?

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:27.840
What?

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.800
Of course, you really <i>must</i> suffer!

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.260
What are they doing?

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:39.890
We'll be moving you all to a new room, 
where the losing team will be penalized!

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.520
Just wait and see!

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.730
<i>Are they going to torture 
them while we watch?</i>

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.980
<i>Or even execute them in front of our eyes?</i>

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:54.360
<i>Damn. I underestimated how 
vicious she could be.</i>

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.710
Welcome, winners!

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.670
You'll be taking a teeny little break,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.050
while the losing team, for their punishment,

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:20.350
will be forced to serve you while 
wearing humiliating outfits!

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:27.560
Don't forget to really show 
off how good the food is!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.690
What's wrong?

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.280
Something on my face?

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.860
Not quite what you expected, was it?

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:36.820
<i>She's utterly...</i>

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.780
Those guys will sit in 
a corner and get water.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.460
How can you guys eat at a time like this?

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.630
I can't even scrape together an appetite.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:49.710
Neither can I.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.800
Well, who knows when we'll 
get another chance to eat?

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.550
I'm so glad the punishment 
was this silly little thing!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.760
You're Akira, aren't you?

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:02.720
You surprised me, how you attacked 
your own teammate during the match...

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.690
I'd <i>love</i> to learn more about you.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.810
The feeling's not mutual.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.320
I don't care about you, or your ability.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.280
Yuuri, can you hand me that plate?

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:15.900
What a pity!

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.240
<i>That woman is dangerous.</i>

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.870
<i>I don't want to have 
anything to do with her.</i>

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.330
Here... ow.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:22.990
What's wrong?

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.700
My wrist's been hurting for a while now.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.290
I guess because of how 
I slammed it into him.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:29.960
Let me see.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.210
What the heck? Don't touch it.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.670
Just hold still and don't move.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.130
There.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.140
Sorry it's just a handkerchief, 
but it should do for now.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:42.890
Hold it as still as you can.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.100
Thanks.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.190
That's a pretty cute hanky, huh?

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:49.520
Shut up.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.400
Hey, you.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.360
Get me some more tea.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.940
R-Right...

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.030
You're acting awfully high-and-mighty.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.860
I'm a winner. I earned it.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.620
But <i>you</i> didn't win.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.750
Hey, he's got a point!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.290
Perhaps you should be a bunny, too.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:17.590
I could ask if they have a spare!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.300
D-Don't you dare, damn it!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:23.260
See? You don't have to let 
that fool bother you.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:24.760
Thanks.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.810
<i>Akira Shiroyanagi. I'm sure he's...</i>

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:31.060
This must be so hard, though...

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.190
For a middle schooler like you.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:35.860
Not at all.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.820
<i>I'm a third-year in high school!</i>

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.910
<i>Excuse me for being short 
and underdeveloped!</i>

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:48.200
Now, it's time to begin the third program!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:52.670
Each team will take a 
different path from here!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.670
Oh, that's right.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.300
Bunny dress-up time was 
just a little bit of fun.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.100
The losing team's penalty 
is still coming up.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.510
See you then, okay?

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:17.020
Each of you will choose a path,
 follow it to the end,

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.400
and follow the instructions 
you receive there.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:21.900
Does that mean...

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.660
...the team's breaking up?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:24.410
Perhaps.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:28.240
Maybe we'll be enemies 
the next time we meet.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.830
That would be an easy win 
for me, against you.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.540
You!

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.210
I'll get you for that!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.880
I don't mind if we meet again as enemies.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.710
It just means we'll all 
have survived that long.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.630
Stay alive, all of you.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.800
Well... later, guys.

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:49.680
I'm going too.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.850
Eeny, meeny, miny...

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:59.190
Yuuri, that handkerchief means a lot to me.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.990
I've had it since I was a kid.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.030
For real?

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.160
If it's that important, you can take it!

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.240
What I mean is...

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:10.490
Make sure you bring it back to me.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.410
Promise you will.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.080
F-Fine.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.790
I'll get it back.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.340
You stay safe, too.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.050
Promise!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.930
There's a seed planted, I hope.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:39.940
<b><<Plagiarist>>

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.410
<b>Mion and Yang's 
\h\h\hNext Episode Preview</b>

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:12.480
Mion and Yang's Next Episode Preview!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:16.040
<b>munch munch</b>

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:15.920
Did you enjoy the fourth episode 
of <i>Battle Game in 5 Seconds<i>

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:17.070
This is real good!</i></i>

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:19.080
Miss Mion! We're on!

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:20.500
<b>munch munch</b>

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:20.560
What are you eating back there?

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:24.160
I'm not eatin'! I'm doin' the important 
preview on an empty stomach!

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:26.300
<b>slurp slurp</b>

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:25.620
You're eating, aren't you?

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:27.610
You're eating noodles or something!

00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:29.840
Am not! Just hang on!

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:30.220
<b>munch munch</b>

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:30.680
Ding!

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.560
What are you doing? What was that "ding"?!

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:34.060
We're running out of time!

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.830
See you for <i>Battle Game 
in 5 Seconds</i>, episode 5!

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:38.670
You <i>are</i> eating, aren't you?!

00:23:38.670 --> 00:23:39.700
Hot, hot, hot!
